# What `docker build` leaves out of the image. Docker never reads .gitignore, and without this
# file it would send this whole folder to the build and `COPY . .` would copy all of it: your
# node_modules (built for your machine, over the image's own install), the database files in
# docker/ and your .env with its secrets, into a layer anyone with the image can read. So this
# follows .gitignore, plus git's own folder; keep the two in step. A pattern here only matches at
# the root of the build context unless it starts with `**/`, so the ones that must also hold in
# folders inside it (other checkouts of the repository live in .claude/worktrees, each with its
# own .env and node_modules) start with `**/`.

# Git, the editor and Claude Code (its other checkouts, with their .env files)
.git
.claude
.github
.vscode
.husky/_

# Dependencies and builds (the image installs and builds its own)
**/node_modules
**/.next
.vercel
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets and local configuration
**/.env*
**/*.pem

# Local database files
docker

# Test output
.vitest
test-results
playwright-report
e2e/.outbox

# Logs and system files
npm-debug.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Personal notes and local files
.personal
.local
# Claude Security scan reports: the folder ignores itself for git only, and a scan's findings
# must never reach an image
**/CLAUDE-SECURITY-*
